SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Candy Cane ***\nRus
 sian Candy Cane — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-
 tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color may w
 ear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only O
 K\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Prop (BA provides): Hoop\nFull Stage Make
 up Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation and powder matching skintone
 \n• Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye sha
 dow over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n• Bla
 ck fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application 
 of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the c
 heeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in th
 e stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• 
 Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark
  Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh ton
 e ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces wit
 h care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptl
 y notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of 
 discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or acces
 sories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refr
 ain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to al
 ter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never appl
 y stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain fr
 om smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the 
 use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any gar
 ment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or b
 everage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remov
 e costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• R
 emove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their
  use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully
  with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• D
 o not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage
  or stain costumes.
