SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nTime: 9:00 PM–9:30 PM.\nIn Performance Co
 stumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDIN
 G RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and ba
 ckstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals 
 (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehea
 rsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\n
 SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and 
 the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/s
 preadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTU
 ME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Candy Cane ***\nRussian Candy Cane — Costume (y
 ou provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes:
  Pink Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; 
 Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\;
  Prop (BA provides): Hoop\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• App
 ly foundation and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shad
 ow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium br
 own eye shadow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply
  mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eye
 liner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty
  so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or 
 tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshado
 w) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Colo
 r may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care 
 Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to preve
 nt damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in th
 e event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how sign
 ificant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang 
 costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor 
 while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launde
 r any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costu
 me and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume
  during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologn
 e while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast memb
 er\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, wit
 h the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned
  dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to s
 ecure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpiece
 s to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to B
 allet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, 
 colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
