SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B @ 2:30 PM – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory – Pro
 duction Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 2:45 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 2:30 PM.\nOn stage: 3:30 PM–4:20 PM.\nACT II
  Cast B Performance.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RUL
 ES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backsta
 ge - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st 
 Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals
  and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJE
 CT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the B
 A portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spread
 sheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / 
 HAIR / MAKEUP — Candy Cane ***\nRussian Candy Cane — Costume (you pr
 ovide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink
  Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeu
 p: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Prop
  (BA provides): Hoop\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply fo
 undation and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow ov
 er entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium brown e
 ye shadow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply masc
 ara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner
  after lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so d
 ancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan o
 n contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to
  darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may
  wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guide
 lines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent da
 mage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the eve
 nt of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significa
 nt\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costu
 mes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while
  in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any
  costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume an
 d shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume duri
 ng its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne whi
 le in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n
 • Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with th
 e exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dre
 ssing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secur
 e head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to
  their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Balle
 t Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colo
 red drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
